1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,253
Your favorite white shirt has turned
yellow, especially

2
00:00:03,263 --> 00:00:06,350
under the arms, and washing doesn't help.

3
00:00:07,315 --> 00:00:08,591
Don't throw it away.

4
00:00:09,555 --> 00:00:12,390
Seven steps bring white clothes back to
bright

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,905
white, without chlorine bleach, for a few
dollars.

6
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:20,305
Stay for step six: it's free, and it
whitens.

7
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:21,919
WikiTube.

8
00:00:22,210 --> 00:00:24,427
Whatever it is, here's how.

9
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,417
Clothes turn yellow because sweat,
deodorant and detergent

10
00:00:28,427 --> 00:00:31,296
residue build up in the fibres, or because

11
00:00:31,306 --> 00:00:33,627
white fabric ages in storage.

12
00:00:33,988 --> 00:00:36,390
Washing doesn't remove that buildup.

13
00:00:36,937 --> 00:00:38,353
A soak does.

14
00:00:39,155 --> 00:00:41,652
Check the care label, test on a hidden

15
00:00:41,662 --> 00:00:46,029
seam, and remember the golden rule: never
mix cleaning

16
00:00:46,039 --> 00:00:47,141
products.

17
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:51,521
You'll need baking soda, white vinegar, an
oxygen

18
00:00:51,531 --> 00:00:55,004
booster powder, liquid dish soap, and a
large

19
00:00:55,014 --> 00:00:56,313
bucket or sink.

20
00:00:57,278 --> 00:01:00,435
Keep chlorine bleach out of this job
completely.

21
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,998
Step one.

22
00:01:02,359 --> 00:01:04,703
Read the care label on each item.

23
00:01:05,668 --> 00:01:08,061
Find out the fabric and the highest water

24
00:01:08,071 --> 00:01:09,649
temperature it can take.

25
00:01:10,614 --> 00:01:13,785
Cotton and polyester blends can usually
handle hot

26
00:01:13,795 --> 00:01:17,686
water, while silk, wool and delicate
fabrics need

27
00:01:17,696 --> 00:01:20,319
special care, so skip those.

28
00:01:20,772 --> 00:01:23,943
Separate your whites by fabric, and keep
colors

29
00:01:23,953 --> 00:01:25,021
out of the soak.

30
00:01:25,985 --> 00:01:29,075
Check every piece for dyes, prints or
metal

31
00:01:29,085 --> 00:01:30,768
buttons that might react.

32
00:01:31,732 --> 00:01:35,609
This simple sorting step prevents most
laundry accidents.

33
00:01:36,063 --> 00:01:38,688
Do this before you start, and you'll avoid

34
00:01:38,698 --> 00:01:41,730
damage, since not every white item will
handle

35
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:44,154
hot water or strong soaks.

36
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,698
Step two.

37
00:01:46,361 --> 00:01:49,114
Lay the stained area flat, and rub in

38
00:01:49,124 --> 00:01:51,679
a few drops of liquid dish soap, or

39
00:01:51,689 --> 00:01:54,301
a paste of baking soda and a little water.

40
00:01:54,661 --> 00:01:57,577
Work it gently into underarm stains and
collars

41
00:01:57,587 --> 00:02:00,108
with an old toothbrush, then let it sit

42
00:02:00,118 --> 00:02:02,242
for fifteen to thirty minutes.

43
00:02:03,044 --> 00:02:05,414
Dish soap breaks down the body oils that

44
00:02:05,424 --> 00:02:10,032
trap the yellow color, while the baking
soda lifts discoloration.

45
00:02:10,834 --> 00:02:13,518
Don't use hot water directly on fresh
sweat

46
00:02:13,528 --> 00:02:16,441
stains, since heat can set some of them.

47
00:02:16,987 --> 00:02:19,276
Old stains might need a second round of

48
00:02:19,286 --> 00:02:23,395
pretreatment, so be patient and repeat if
needed.

49
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:24,931
Step three.

50
00:02:25,292 --> 00:02:27,999
Fill a basin with hot water, as hot

51
00:02:28,009 --> 00:02:29,749
as the care label allows.

52
00:02:30,551 --> 00:02:33,049
Add half a cup of baking soda, and

53
00:02:33,059 --> 00:02:35,067
stir until it dissolves.

54
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:38,390
Add the clothes, and let them soak for

55
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,140
one to two hours.

56
00:02:41,105 --> 00:02:45,632
Baking soda softens the water and lifts
stains and odors.

57
00:02:46,179 --> 00:02:48,665
Afterward, you can rinse and add a cup

58
00:02:48,675 --> 00:02:51,286
of white vinegar to a fresh rinse bath,

59
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:54,955
for a few minutes, which removes soap
residue.

60
00:02:55,757 --> 00:02:58,580
Don't combine vinegar and the oxygen
booster in

61
00:02:58,590 --> 00:02:59,715
the same soak.

62
00:03:00,378 --> 00:03:02,562
Keep the basin covered if there are
children

63
00:03:02,572 --> 00:03:06,484
or pets around, and always rinse the
clothes well afterward.

64
00:03:07,033 --> 00:03:08,042
Step four.

65
00:03:08,705 --> 00:03:12,596
For stubborn yellowing, dissolve oxygen
booster powder in

66
00:03:12,606 --> 00:03:16,158
hot water, following the instructions on
the package.

67
00:03:16,704 --> 00:03:20,314
A common amount is one scoop per gallon of
water.

68
00:03:21,464 --> 00:03:24,459
Wear gloves, because it can irritate skin.

69
00:03:25,423 --> 00:03:28,478
Submerge the clothes completely, and leave
them to

70
00:03:28,488 --> 00:03:31,100
soak for four to eight hours or overnight,

71
00:03:31,228 --> 00:03:32,667
stirring now and then.

72
00:03:33,817 --> 00:03:37,718
Oxygen boosters release oxygen when
dissolved in water,

73
00:03:37,742 --> 00:03:41,677
which breaks down stains without the
harshness of chlorine bleach.

74
00:03:42,827 --> 00:03:45,252
Never use it on silk or wool.

75
00:03:45,613 --> 00:03:48,018
Never put the oxygen booster in a closed

76
00:03:48,028 --> 00:03:51,557
container, because it releases gas as it
works.

77
00:03:52,707 --> 00:03:54,877
A loose lid is enough.

78
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:56,477
Step five.

79
00:03:56,768 --> 00:03:59,231
Wring out the clothes, and run them
through

80
00:03:59,241 --> 00:04:01,797
the washing machine on the warmest cycle
that

81
00:04:01,807 --> 00:04:03,130
the label allows.

82
00:04:04,094 --> 00:04:07,599
Use your regular detergent, but don't
overdo it.

83
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:12,928
Too much detergent leaves residue that
makes whites look dull.

84
00:04:13,893 --> 00:04:16,344
Add half a cup of baking soda directly

85
00:04:16,354 --> 00:04:18,339
to the drum to boost cleaning.

86
00:04:19,489 --> 00:04:23,075
Wash whites only, and don't overload the
machine,

87
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:25,026
so the water can circulate.

88
00:04:26,176 --> 00:04:29,623
Before drying, check the stained area in
good light.

89
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:32,354
Use the sink or a bucket to rinse

90
00:04:32,364 --> 00:04:35,222
any soaked items first, and wring them out

91
00:04:35,232 --> 00:04:37,982
gently to avoid stretching the fabric.

92
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:39,751
Step six.

93
00:04:40,297 --> 00:04:42,769
Sunlight is a natural whitener.

94
00:04:43,316 --> 00:04:46,023
Hang your clothes outside, or lay them
flat

95
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:48,830
on a clean surface, in direct sun.

96
00:04:49,632 --> 00:04:52,281
The UV light helps fade yellow tones in

97
00:04:52,291 --> 00:04:53,753
cotton and linen.

98
00:04:54,206 --> 00:04:56,449
Avoid the dryer until you're sure the
stain

99
00:04:56,459 --> 00:05:00,370
is gone, because heat can lock in any
remaining color.

100
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:03,484
If you can't dry outside, hang them near

101
00:05:03,494 --> 00:05:04,620
a bright window.

102
00:05:05,166 --> 00:05:07,734
If the yellowing is still visible, repeat
the

103
00:05:07,744 --> 00:05:11,052
soak, as old stains sometimes need two
rounds.

104
00:05:12,202 --> 00:05:15,324
Direct sun for a couple of hours is
usually enough.

105
00:05:15,685 --> 00:05:18,543
Bring delicate items inside before they
get too

106
00:05:18,553 --> 00:05:19,783
dry and stiff.

107
00:05:20,333 --> 00:05:21,458
Step seven.

108
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:24,244
Prevent yellowing in the future.

109
00:05:24,605 --> 00:05:28,691
Wash whites separately, and wash sweaty
items promptly.

110
00:05:29,841 --> 00:05:32,641
Use the right amount of detergent, and add

111
00:05:32,651 --> 00:05:35,250
an extra rinse if you have hard water.

112
00:05:36,401 --> 00:05:39,119
Skip fabric softener on whites, as it can

113
00:05:39,129 --> 00:05:40,103
leave a film.

114
00:05:41,254 --> 00:05:43,542
Choose a deodorant that doesn't leave a
heavy

115
00:05:43,552 --> 00:05:46,431
residue, and let it dry before dressing.

116
00:05:47,581 --> 00:05:50,265
Store clothes clean and fully dry, away
from

117
00:05:50,275 --> 00:05:54,117
direct light and cardboard boxes, which
can cause yellowing.

118
00:05:55,081 --> 00:05:58,253
A monthly maintenance wash with baking
soda keeps

119
00:05:58,263 --> 00:06:01,675
whites bright and stops yellowing from
taking hold.

120
00:06:02,233 --> 00:06:05,437
If the yellow is still there, think about
the cause.

121
00:06:06,239 --> 00:06:09,663
Sweat and body oil stains respond to
soaking,

122
00:06:10,024 --> 00:06:12,684
but a repeat soak is often needed, so

123
00:06:12,694 --> 00:06:13,994
do a second round.

124
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:17,572
Orange or brown spots may be rust, which

125
00:06:17,582 --> 00:06:20,405
needs a rust remover made for fabric, used

126
00:06:20,415 --> 00:06:21,633
as the label says.

127
00:06:21,994 --> 00:06:24,721
Test any product on a hidden seam first.

128
00:06:25,175 --> 00:06:27,719
Very old yellowing in aged fabric can be

129
00:06:27,729 --> 00:06:31,316
permanent, and more scrubbing will only
wear the fibers.

130
00:06:31,867 --> 00:06:34,467
Some white items are better left to a
professional.

131
00:06:34,828 --> 00:06:39,160
Silk, wool, lace and anything labeled dry

132
00:06:39,170 --> 00:06:42,176
clean only can be ruined by a hot soak.

133
00:06:42,537 --> 00:06:45,859
The same goes for wedding dresses,
christening gowns

134
00:06:45,869 --> 00:06:50,117
and family heirlooms, where a mistake
cannot be undone.

135
00:06:50,571 --> 00:06:52,639
Tell the cleaner what the stain is and

136
00:06:52,649 --> 00:06:53,890
how old it is.

137
00:06:54,251 --> 00:06:56,714
A good cleaner can often lift a stain

138
00:06:56,724 --> 00:06:59,303
that has resisted home care, and will say

139
00:06:59,313 --> 00:07:00,949
honestly if it cannot.

140
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:06,044
Many yellow underarm stains form when
sweat reacts

141
00:07:06,054 --> 00:07:08,991
with aluminum compounds in antiperspirant.

142
00:07:09,538 --> 00:07:12,186
A thin undershirt takes the sweat in place

143
00:07:12,196 --> 00:07:13,403
of your white shirt.

144
00:07:13,949 --> 00:07:16,645
Rinse fresh stains in cold water as soon

145
00:07:16,655 --> 00:07:17,640
as you can.

146
00:07:18,605 --> 00:07:21,472
Wash white shirts after one or two wears,

147
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:24,815
because body oils build up and darken
slowly.

148
00:07:25,269 --> 00:07:29,053
Do not overload the machine, so dirt can
rinse out.

149
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,619
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

150
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:34,196
First, mixing products.

151
00:07:34,557 --> 00:07:38,320
Never combine chlorine bleach with
vinegar, ammonia or

152
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:42,080
other cleaners, as it can create dangerous
fumes.

153
00:07:43,044 --> 00:07:47,467
Second, using too much detergent, which
leaves a dulling film.

154
00:07:48,013 --> 00:07:50,778
And third, drying the item in a hot

155
00:07:50,788 --> 00:07:53,759
dryer before the stain is completely gone.

156
00:07:54,909 --> 00:07:57,860
Heat sets stains, and then they are far

157
00:07:57,870 --> 00:07:59,216
harder to remove.

158
00:08:00,367 --> 00:08:04,174
Soak, check, and only then dry.

159
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:09,224
Patience, gentle products and sunshine do
most of the work.

160
00:08:09,767 --> 00:08:10,939
Let's recap.

161
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:13,098
Check the labels and sort.

162
00:08:14,063 --> 00:08:15,885
Pretreat the yellow stains.

163
00:08:16,176 --> 00:08:18,625
Soak in hot water with baking soda.

164
00:08:18,986 --> 00:08:22,201
Try an oxygen booster soak for stubborn
yellowing.

165
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:24,697
Wash on a warm cycle.

166
00:08:25,847 --> 00:08:27,077
Dry in the sun.

167
00:08:27,624 --> 00:08:30,746
And keep whites white with a few simple
habits.

168
00:08:31,896 --> 00:08:35,970
Seven steps, mostly waiting, and clothes
that look new again.

169
00:08:36,517 --> 00:08:38,237
Do it once a month for whites that

170
00:08:38,247 --> 00:08:39,871
stay bright all year.

171
00:08:41,021 --> 00:08:43,298
Bonus sections cover what to do if the

172
00:08:43,308 --> 00:08:46,280
yellow stays, when to call a dry cleaner,

173
00:08:46,571 --> 00:08:49,391
and the habits that stop new yellowing.

174
00:08:49,933 --> 00:08:54,182
That's how you whiten yellowed white
clothes without harsh bleach.

175
00:08:54,543 --> 00:08:57,180
If your shirts are bright again, subscribe
to

176
00:08:57,190 --> 00:09:01,845
WikiTube, because we publish a new how-to
every single day.

177
